course: dictionary
lesson: 2072
title: Constantly
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Constantly means all the time, again and again, without stopping. Look at the words around it for clues. «If an older sibling teases you constantly, tell them how it makes you feel» means the teasing keeps happening, not just once.
explain: Constantly can also mean always in the same way, without changing. «The Sun constantly blows out charged particles called the solar wind» tells us the Sun never stops doing this. Try the swap: «The Sun always blows out charged particles» still makes sense, so always is a good match.
explain: Watch for «constant», which is a close cousin. A constant speed stays the same and does not speed up or slow down. Ask yourself: is this word about something that keeps happening, or something that stays the same?
fact: Constantly means all the time, or again and again without stopping.
fact: Constantly can also mean always in the same way, without changing.
fact: «Cubs play constantly, chasing tails and wrestling» means the cubs play again and again, all the time.
fact: Phrases to know: constantly changing, constantly moving, constantly asking.
fact: A quick check is to swap in «all the time» or «always». If the sentence still makes sense, you have the right meaning.
exercise: «The river is constantly moving, never still.» What does constantly mean here? | Once in a while | *Without stopping | Under the water | Very slowly
exercise: Find the phrase that means about the same as constantly. | just once | *all the time | at intervals | now and then
exercise: Maya says a constant speed means the car speeds up. What is true? | *A constant speed stays the same, without speeding up or slowing down | A constant speed means the car is always going faster | A constant speed means the car has stopped
test: «The Sun constantly blows out charged particles.» What does constantly tell us? | *It keeps happening all the time, without stopping | It happens only at night | It happens near the planets only | It happens once, at the start
test: Which word is the best swap for constantly in «Ravi is constantly asking questions»? | *always | quietly | rarely | slowly
exam: Which is the best way to check the meaning of constantly? | Look only at the first letter | Skip it and never come back to it | Count the letters in the word | *Swap in «all the time» or «always» and see if the sentence still makes sense
